      "sameCluster": false,
      "similar": "Both questions ask how many distances a set of points can determine. They connect geometric structure with quantitative information about distance.",
      "different": "Family 073 concerns possibly fractal compact sets and the measure of their distance sets. Family 166 concerns a finite collection of points and a lower bound on the number of distinct distances. Continuous size and finite counting are different notions."
    },
